2. Project overview 
2.1 Project Background
As the world embraces the digital, it follows that job recruitment and application has also moved increasingly online. Millions of job listings and jobseekers are handled by online platforms like Seek and Indeed, and this is only growing. Through these platforms, however, candidates struggle to find roles truly relevant to their qualifications and experience. Additionally, employers and businesses are overwhelmed by high volumes of applications that do not necessarily match their requirements.

This issue has intensified over COVID-19, with available remote and hybrid work meaning candidates have a greater pool of jobs to apply to globally. While most industry-standard platforms have integrated AI into their platforms, employers and candidates still remain frustrated during the hiring process. (Yeyati and Seyal, 2025) This highlights that these AI-powered talent matching systems can still be developed and improved to reduce instances of candidates receiving non-ideal jobs and employers being overwhelmed by under-qualified applications.  

To solve this problem, the Intelligent Talent Matching Platform integrates a two-way recommendation engine, through the inclusion of AI and ML-driven matching, to improve on the results of current solutions. This engine both recommends relevant jobs to candidates and recommends relevant candidates to employers. This aims to reduce the effort needed by both parties during the recruitment and job-hunting process.  
2.2 Problem Definition 
For Candidates
Waste time applying to roles they are unqualified/ are not a good fit for
Profiles are static with no way to highlight strengths towards job applications and employers
For Employers
Receive a large amount of irrelevant applications
Cannot quickly shortlist candidates by multiple criteria concurrently
For both:
Keyword searches do not produce contextually relevant results

The problems of these users highlight common issues in existing job hunting applications which this system design aims to solve. 
